<title>USA: Pfizer to buy back $2 bln worth of common.</title>
<headline>Pfizer to buy back $2 bln worth of common.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pfizer Inc said on Thursday its board had authorized the repurchase of up to $2.0 billion worth of its currently issued common stock.</p>
<p>The buyback will be made from time to time over the next 24 months in the open market or private transactions, the company said.</p>
<p>Pfizer now has 625 million shares of common stock outstanding. Its shares were up 1-1/2 at 78-7/8 in late-morning trading.</p>
<p>Shares bought back will be held in the company's treasury, available for general corporate purposes, Pfizer said.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1733</p>
